From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:01:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D224 server: an unframed terminal client's input keeps the
 terminal's size

Upstream: a persistent terminal socket without framed input (`input_protocol` other than 1, as clients before
framed input connect) sends every keystroke to the daemon as `input` with the terminal size it read when it
attached. Input promotes its sender at that size, so once the terminal has been resized (through the API, or by
another client) the next keystroke from such a client resizes it back to the stale size.
Fixed: the handler follows the terminal's `resized` events and sends the latest size with an unframed client's
input; framed clients still send their own.
Scenarios: pty-persistent.test.ts "persistent terminal websocket: control, observers, input and exit" (the
observer's keystroke no longer resizes 60x10 back to 40x6)
Upstream tests: packages/server/test/persistent-pty.test.ts adds a test

